diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-serial-sy108-mcu b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-serial-sy108-mcu
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b9b3e41df
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-serial-sy108-mcu
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../event
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+                Read-only SY108 MCU event snapshot. It reports "none" before
+                any event, otherwise "seq=<number> kind=poweroff|usb-reset".
+                A power request awaiting orderly shutdown takes precedence
+                over the latest USB event, including during early boot.
+
+                The driver emits a change uevent with MCU_EVENT and MCU_SEQ.
+                USB ACKs are sent by the driver before the uevent. A pending
+                power ACK is attempted only from the SYS_POWER_OFF blocking
+                reboot notifier, before UART device shutdown. There is no
+                userspace ACK attribute. A restart does not send a power ACK.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../firmware_version
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+                Read-only MCU firmware version returned by the UART protocol.
+                A transport error is returned to the reader.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../status
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+                Read-only transport counters, including received frames,
+                protocol errors, ADC requests, timeouts, MCU events and ACK
+                attempts. last_ack_error is the result of the last UART write.
+                A completed write and transmit drain do not prove receipt by
+                the MCU. ADC3..5 use the standard IIO raw voltage attributes.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-sprd-efuse-uid b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-sprd-efuse-uid
deleted file mode 100644
index d7b057a9b..000000000
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-sprd-efuse-uid
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,19 +0,0 @@
-What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/63400000.efuse/soc_uid
-Date:           October 2026
-Contact:        UDX710 board maintainers
-Description:
-                Read-only SoC UID for the Orca eFuse variant. The file mode is
-                0400 and its size is exactly 8 bytes. It contains two
-                little-endian 32-bit words: physical eFuse block 0 followed by
-                block 1, with bit 31 cleared in each word. The controller reads
-                both blocks in double mode, matching the board's original
-                U-Boot READ_UID response. Partial reads are supported.
-
-                Hardware lock, clock and controller failures return an error
-                without exposing partial UID bytes. All-zero or all-one masked
-                UID values return ENODATA. This interface never programs eFuse.
-
-                The existing orca-public-efuse calibration provider retains
-                its 180-byte aperture at physical blocks 2 through 46. Its
-                offset 0 is not the UID. CONFIG_NVMEM_SYSFS is not required for
-                this dedicated attribute.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-udx710-cellular-session b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-udx710-cellular-session
index 8e84f42c6..ff38c59df 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-udx710-cellular-session
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-udx710-cellular-session
@@ -1,23 +1,3 @@
-What:           /sys/class/spipe/<name>/session
-Date:           October 2026
-Contact:        UDX710 AP-side port maintainers
-Description:
-                Read-only ASCII line: "1 dst channel generation state\n".
-                Values are decimal u32; version is currently 1. Generation
-                is the driver's SBUF software generation, wrapping at 2^32.
-                State 0 means idle/unready, 1 means the SBUF transport handshake
-                is ready, and 2 means stopping. This is not CP authentication,
-                HALO, SIM, registration or data-session readiness. Reads only
-                snapshot existing software fields under state_lock; they do not
-                consume SMSG/SBUF, inspect MMIO, or change any state.
-                All character nodes on one channel report the same snapshot.
-                The fixed UDX710 PSCP nodes are spipe_lte2 (dst5/channel4),
-                stty_lte0 (dst5/channel6), and snv_lte (dst5/channel40).
-                A userspace owner may arm a baseline after observing state1;
-                then any generation difference (equality comparison, not order),
-                state loss, read error or malformed record invalidates its old
-                descriptors. Close/reopen alone does not prove SIPA DMA drain.
-
 What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/89600000.sipa-dele/cp_session
 Date:           October 2026
 Contact:        UDX710 AP-side port maintainers
